[{"client_msg_id":"4075c5c4-e7b4-497c-8221-b5ddd8958389","type":"message","user":"U01D9BALEKU","text":"\u003chttp://www.n-seiryo.ac.jp/~nonaka/seminar/l09162/page1.htm|http://www.n-seiryo.ac.jp/~nonaka/seminar/l09162/page1.htm\u003e","ts":"1625487925.206900","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"IREK"}]},{"client_msg_id":"27221f02-799d-4506-9ccc-94ec2b383c90","type":"message","user":"U01D9BALEKU","text":"\u0026gt; タイ・ラン：You…can't defeat me.  You… you're just a big… fat… panda!\n\u0026gt; \n\u0026gt; 「お前に…おれは倒せん　お前…お前なんかただの……デブパンダだ！」\n\u0026gt; \n\u0026gt; ポー：I'm a not a big fat panda.  I'm the big fat panda.\n\u0026gt; \n\u0026gt; 「ただのデブパンダ？元祖デブパンダだ」","ts":"1625487917.206700","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"wiNd"}]},{"client_msg_id":"2c2abc98-50c4-49dc-9fb0-40838ae1cf38","type":"message","user":"U01D9BALEKU","text":"話の流れとはややずれるけどa/theの説明でお〜と思った例","ts":"1625487909.206500","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"W0iq8"}]},{"client_msg_id":"3e7a813f-fb5e-4656-be7f-c4b56999b21f","type":"message","user":"U8R597E9H","text":"happend to でたまたま〜動詞だった　なのか。勉強になる。","ts":"1625475893.205700","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"sz1P4"}]},{"client_msg_id":"db7d4ea4-8f20-465e-bb82-34051702ee53","type":"message","user":"UG6DF6W87","text":"// 冠詞、関数 `hoge()` を指すときにそれだけだと冠詞付けないけど `hoge() function` みたいに書くと the をつけたくなるけどあってるのかしらん","ts":"1625475548.205300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"nqrm"}]},{"client_msg_id":"52b7ab51-757b-4788-ae25-deabe138c2c2","type":"message","user":"UEACRCY0Z","text":"a/the についてはぼくはこんな理解です。\n\nI happened to have a pen, so I signed with the pen.","ts":"1625475329.203900","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"kKLYY"}]},{"client_msg_id":"c9349207-ffce-4cd1-8a0d-9238aac58b96","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"a number と the number については、前者が単なるイディオムなんではないかと思った","ts":"1625466346.201300","team":"T03C4RC8V","reactions":[{"name":"wakaru","count":3,"users":["UFHQ7TNT0","U01AQ5BFNLX","UEACRCY0Z"]}],"replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"hPQ"}]},{"client_msg_id":"03141ad6-6086-4461-8a51-a6de351fa364","type":"message","user":"UERCTTT8B","text":"それであっているっぽいですね \u003chttps://okmount.hatenablog.com/entry/20101221/p1\u003e","ts":"1625466127.200400","thread_ts":"1625465172.198300","attachments":[{"fallback":"学習する機械、学習しない人間 Next Generation: 「特定のものを指す名詞には the をつける」 → ダウト - 学習する機械、学習しない人間 Next Generation","id":1,"title":"「特定のものを指す名詞には the をつける」 → ダウト - 学習する機械、学習しない人間 Next Generation","title_link":"https://okmount.hatenablog.com/entry/20101221/p1","text":"英語の冠詞の the の使い方でよく間違えられるのだが、「特定のものを指す名詞には the をつける」のではない。この勘違いに基づいて書かれた文章は、往々にして読み手に「その the のついた名詞が指しているものがどれなのかわからない」という混乱を生じさせる。どういうことか。今回はそれについて書いてみる。参考元: わかりやすい英語冠詞講義作者: 石田秀雄出版社/メーカー: 大修館書店発売日: 2002/03/01メディア: 単行本購入: 9人 クリック: 42回この商品を含むブログ (11件) を見る英語の冠詞の使い方について、非常に詳しく解説している。オススメ。 本記事はほぼこの本に基づいて…","thumb_url":"https://images-fe.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/519F37EH44L._SL160_.jpg","blocks":null,"ts":1292857200,"service_name":"学習する機械、学習しない人間 Next Generation","service_icon":"https://okmount.hatenablog.com/icon/touch","thumb_width":107,"thumb_height":160,"from_url":"https://okmount.hatenablog.com/entry/20101221/p1","original_url":"https://okmount.hatenablog.com/entry/20101221/p1"}],"subtype":"thread_broadcast","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"b=qov"}],"root":{"client_msg_id":"651f6fb1-a914-48c5-ad06-17cea0da2c3d","type":"message","user":"U01AQ5BFNLX","text":"theは話し手が共通認識だろうと思っているものにつく","ts":"1625465172.198300","thread_ts":"1625465172.19830